C(11093,'open on the pages','A','RS-TORI','R-SGA3XII','The deferral is genuine. XII1.4 specifies the artinian-base or local-base/reductive-group cases and points to ExposéXIV for containment in a maximal torus. It is not an arbitrary-base universal containment theorem.','SGA3 publication1970',statement='The stated torus-containment theorem is deferred to XIV under either the artinian-base hypotheses in the exposé or the local-base/reductive-group alternative; the exact deleted-versus-inserted conjunction remains a reading alarm.',confidence='medium')
C(11058,'proof sketched','A','RS-TORI','R-SGA3XII','XII1.8 proves the centralizer dimension bound by enlarging the torus over an algebraic closure and reversing centralizer inclusion. This is the completed proof fragment at c56:33.','SGA3 publication1970',statement='For a smooth affine algebraic groupG over a field and a torusT⊂G, its nilpotent/Cartan rankρn(G) is at most dimC_G(T).',suffix='b',scans=[14,33],lines=[{'file':'SA18_texts/pro/MPL_11_043-058+56_transcription.tex','start':1151,'end':1162},{'file':'SA18_texts/pro/MPL_11_043-058+56_transcription.tex','start':1740,'end':1743}])
C(11037,'proof sketched','B','RS-QUADRIC','R-SGA7XV','SGA7 XV2.1 gives the same projective-cone cohomology calculation. The positive-degree product has the extra hyperplane factor; identifying only graded groups would omit this part of the source.','SGA7II1973',statement='For a projective cone over a connected smooth projective complexX with hyperplane classh, H⁰(Cproj)=Z and H^i(Cproj)≅H^(i−2)(X)(−1) fori>0; under this identification the product of positive-degree classes corresponds, up to the fixed section convention, to multiplication byh times their product onX.',proof='research/root_proofs.md R4',suffix='b',scans=[11])
D(11103,'e','proved there','A','The geometric form follows from the local inequality at the two generic points; the dominance condition identifies those points correctly.','For a morphism f:X→Y of locally noetherian schemes, an irreducible closedY′ and an irreducible componentX′ of f⁻¹(Y′) dominatingY′, codim_X X′≤codim_Y Y′.')
D(11103,'f','proved there','A','The nonvanishing-at-generic-points condition excludes height0 components; Krull’s principal ideal theorem then gives height exactly1.','If a global functionf on a locally noetherian scheme is nonzero at every generic point, every irreducible component of its zero set has codimension1.')
D(11104,'d','open on the pages','A','The inserted residue-transcendence correction is the correct pointwise formula for finite-type schemes over a field; at a closed point that transcendence degree is0.','For X finite type overk and x∈X, dim_xX=dimO_(X,x)+trdeg_kκ(x). The local topological dimension is the maximum of component dimensions throughx.')
D(11108,'d','proved there','A','EGA0IV14.2.2(iv) gives the same zero-codimension characterization, independent of the noetherianT0 hypotheses needed for the separate dimension0 assertion.','A closed subsetY⊂X has codimension0 iff it contains an irreducible component ofX.')
D(11101,'c','stated without proof','C','The source asserts equivalences for globally finitely presented algebras and modules underα alone. The opened Stein references prove these comparisons under their analytic/global-generation hypotheses; they do not prove this unrestricted ringed-space statement. The source’s later filtered-limit/coherence questions leave exactly that extension uncompleted.','Under conditionα(exactΓ on finite global presentations), the draft asserts that finitely presented A-algebras correspond to globally finitely presented O-algebras, and likewise their finitely presented modules. The passage from finite O-presentations to polynomial-degree filtrations needs the additional commutation/coherence assumptions examined on scans10,12.',refs='R-Benoist2026 R-BuchweitzFlenner2003 R-LSY2012',search='RS-STEIN',date='Analytic comparisons2003/2026; exact unrestricted extension not located by2026-11-19',confidence='medium')

# Correctly identify exact certificate groups, rather than ambiguous descriptive names.
certificate_keys={11009:['P1_diagonals'],11010:['P1_diagonals'],11014:['P1_diagonals'],11015:['P1_diagonals'],11024:['sorted_cone'],11025:['separation_missing_nonzero'],11038:['quadrics','quadric_Q0'],11041:['quadrics','quadric_Q0'],11042:['quadric_middle_lattice'],11045:['quadric_middle_lattice'],11047:['quadric_middle_lattice'],11049:['quadrics','quadric_Q0'],11050:['quadric_middle_lattice'],11052:['quadrics'],11053:['quadrics'],11054:['quadrics'],11064:['nested_tori'],11065:['Gm_Ga_group_law'],11081:['SW_rankzero_product'],11082:['Clifford_normalization_alarm'],11084:['real_signature_binary_check'],11096:['RP2_LemmaA_counterexample'],11110:['literal_torus','alternative_torus']}
for c in claims:
    n=int(c['items'][0].split('-')[-1])
    if n in certificate_keys:
        c['computation']['certificate_keys']=certificate_keys[n]
        events.append(dict(statement_id=c['id'],date='2026-11-19',who=WHO,type='computation or formal certificate',outcome='Executed scripts/root_certificates.py; exact output keys: '+', '.join(certificate_keys[n])+'. Scope is the stated model/formula, with the general argument separately recorded.'))

